Package: wsh-qemu-rdp
Architecture: any
Depends: openssl,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: qemu-server (>= 9.2.20+wsh8),
Description: RDP server for the D-Bus display of Proxmox VE VMs (qemu-rdp)
 qemu-rdp from Marc-André Lureau's qemu-display project: an RDP server
 (IronRDP) that serves the screen, keyboard, mouse and sound of a QEMU
 started with -display dbus. With the wsh-pve qemu-server, a VM gets that
 display with 'vga: <type>,display=dbus' (sound with 'audio0: ...,driver=dbus'),
 on a D-Bus bus of its own (wsh-dbus-display@<vmid>.service).
 .
 The unit wsh-qemu-rdp@<vmid>.service runs qemu-rdp for one VM, as the
 unprivileged user wsh-qemu-rdp (group wsh-display), started and stopped with
 the VM's bus once enabled (systemctl enable --now wsh-qemu-rdp@<vmid>).
 /etc/wsh-qemu-rdp/<vmid>.conf, written at the first start, holds the address
 (127.0.0.1 by default), the port (20000 + VMID by default) and the RDP user
 and password (generated); without a certificate of your own, the node gets a
 self-signed one. Clients log in with NLA (CredSSP over TLS).
 .
 RemoteFX and bitmap codecs (no H.264), sound through rdpsnd (PCM, or Opus for
 clients that take it), resizing the guest's screen from the client, text
 clipboard. Mouse movement needs an absolute pointer in the guest (PVE's USB
 tablet); without one only the buttons arrive.
